Touch this file to ask the runner to regenerate the visual baselines.

Any commit that changes this file — on any branch — runs
.github/workflows/visual-baselines.yml, which rebuilds
tests/visual/__screenshots__/linux/ on the ubuntu runner and commits the result
back to the branch you pushed. Nothing else in the repo triggers it, so a regen
is always something you asked for on purpose.

Use it after a change that legitimately moves pixels, once you have LOOKED at
what moved. Regenerating to make CI go green is how a real regression gets
baked into the baseline it was supposed to be caught by.

The equivalent button, when you can reach the Actions UI:
Actions → "Update visual baselines" → Run workflow.

